From 58242fa6740fe9db3d70e75cf0df3c5d2a8fcfb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:07:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 56/76] camss: Capture the sensor's phase detection stream

A sensor with a metadata stream beside the image, found by CameraSensorRaw
(on this platform, a phase detection stream), gets a second capture path:
the CSI phy and the CSI decoder route it, with the V4L2 streams API, from
the decoder's second source pad to the next RDI of the same VFE, whose
video node captures it as metadata (opened for META_CAPTURE, as the node
also offers video capture). The image keeps the default route, so its
path is configured as before. Where the kernel cannot route the stream,
the camera runs without it.

The pipeline allocates the PD buffers, shares them with the ISP's IPA and
hands it each completed buffer with its sequence number, queueing it
again once the IPA is done. Phase detection is optional throughout: if
the IPA cannot use the stream, it is not started. The soft ISP and the
OPE forward the calls to the soft IPA, which logs each buffer's combined
phase at debug level.

Also log receiver-unsupported media bus codes at debug level: sensors on
the common raw sensor model offer generic raw codes that CAMSS cannot
capture, next to the Bayer ones it can.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
